description:
## Finding

`pkix-chain-simple/src/lib.rs:466`:

```rust
const _: () = assert!(
    MAX_INTERMEDIATES <= u8::MAX as usize,
    "MAX_INTERMEDIATES must fit in u8"
);
```

Inside `verify_simple()`, this `const _` assertion appears mid-function after several statements. Clippy: `clippy::items_after_statements`.

## Why this matters

`const _` is hoisted to compile time regardless of where it's written, so placing it inside the function body suggests it's "guarding the next statement" — but it actually fires at the top of the crate. Readers may wonder if this is a runtime check that conditionally executes.

## Fix

Hoist to module scope:

```rust
// At the top of the module, near MAX_INTERMEDIATES definition:
const _: () = assert!(
    MAX_INTERMEDIATES <= u8::MAX as usize,
    "MAX_INTERMEDIATES must fit in u8"
);

// inside verify_simple(): just use MAX_INTERMEDIATES as u8 with the existing #[allow]
```

## Priority

P4 — readability nit.
